# 010 — Sync README and handoff with the code — done

**Type:** docs · **Priority:** medium · **Status:** done (2026-10-03)
**Affects:** `README.md`, the handoff document

## Discrepancies

| Where | Stated | Actual |
|---|---|---|
| README, "How to Build" | `chmod +x patch_008_preemptive.sh` / `./patch_008_preemptive.sh` | the file does not exist; the build is `01_prepare_env.sh` + `02_build.sh` |
| Handoff, section 3 | "the `fix_stable_boot.sh` script" | the file does not exist; `02_build.sh` is the current one |
| README, "Event Model" | "Hardware interrupts (IDT) for timing and keyboard input, combined with software interrupts (`int 0x80`)" | neither IDT nor `int 0x80` exist in the code; the keyboard is port polling; see [004](004-apic-idt-interrupts.done), [005](005-syscalls.done) |
| README, "Toolchain" | "utilizing `naked_functions` and `abi_x86_interrupt`" | neither feature gate is used |
| README | path `/usr/share/ovmf/OVMF.fd` | on Debian/Ubuntu: `/usr/share/OVMF/OVMF_CODE_4M.fd` (+ `OVMF_VARS_4M.fd`); the repository uses a local `OVMF.fd` (gitignored) |
| README, title | "Iain M. Banks supposed # MIND CORE" | merged lines/typo |
| Handoff, section 1 | the bootloader reads files from FAT32 | `include_bytes!` — [006](006-bootloader-load-from-fat32.done) |
| Handoff, section 1 | font and primitive rendering | absent — [007](007-kernel-font-and-primitives.done) |
| Handoff, section 1 | switch to userspace after a delay or on a key press | only on space — [008](008-kernel-timeout-handoff.done) |
| Handoff, section 2 | "`.bss` without `linker.ld`" | `linker.ld` exists; the problem is in objcopy/allocation — [003](003-bss-and-heap-allocator.done) |
| Handoff, section 3 | objcopy dumps `.text/.rodata/.data` | all alloc content is dumped — [001](001-flat-binary-entry-offset-and-got-call.done) |

## Plan

1. README: rewrite the "Event Model" section as "Step 0: polling; interrupts — roadmap", remove the nonexistent script, add a Linux command for running QEMU with `OVMF_CODE_4M.fd` + `OVMF_VARS_4M.fd` (`-drive if=pflash,...`), fix the title.
2. Put the handoff into the repository (`docs/handoff.md`) and update it according to the matrix in [knowledge/04](../knowledge/04-handoff-vs-code-matrix.md).
3. Add links to `knowledge/` and `issues/` to the README.
4. Add `03_run_qemu.sh` for Linux (counterpart of the `.bat`).

## Acceptance criteria

Every statement in README/handoff either matches the code or is marked as "roadmap" with a link to an issue.

## Resolution

README is maintained together with the code (sections Current Runtime, System services, IPC, libmind SDK, tests); the handoff document is not part of the repository; `knowledge/04` is kept as a historical matrix. Further documentation work is tracked in [ROADMAP](../ROADMAP.md).

## Audit (2026-10-04)

Done. Plan items not carried out: the OVMF pflash command, links to `issues/` and `knowledge/`, a Linux `03_run_qemu.sh`.

Follow-up (2026-10-04, [033](033-audit-and-supervision-follow-ups.done)): the Linux launcher `03_run_qemu.sh` (with the OVMF pflash fallback) and the README links to `issues/` and `knowledge/` were added in 033.
